{
    "Description": {
        "Id": "forceevent_co_LutefiskAmmoSmokey_4t",
        "Name": "What's That Smell?",
        "Details": "You come across Jarl in the Armory aboard the <i>Argo</i>. Materials are spread across several tables, with open cans of lutefisk, containers of fermented goat's milk, mortar powder, mixing equipment, and various other components arranged around him.\r\n\r\nThe air is pungent. The unmistakable aroma of fermented goat's milk and open cans of lutefisk hangs heavily in the Armory, mixed with the sharp chemical smell of mortar powder. Beneath it all is the surprisingly pleasant smell of burning wood.\r\n\r\nYou look around until you spot the source. A small device sits on one of the tables, quietly producing a thin stream of smoke.\r\n\r\n\"What's that?\"\r\n\r\nJarl looks up from his work. \"The Smoker.\"\r\n\r\nYou look at the device again. \"You're smoking the ammunition?\"\r\n\r\nJarl shakes his head. \"Not exactly. The Smoker doesn't burn wood. It produces a smokey residue that I can incorporate into the Lutefisk Ammo. When the mortar shell explodes, the residue disperses and obscures the surrounding area.\"\r\n\r\nYou eye the mixture being prepared on the nearest table. \"So we're making smoked lutefisk that explodes.\"\r\n\r\nJarl smiles. \"Smokey Lutefisk Ammo. More accurately, ammunition that leaves a dense obscuring cloud when it detonates.\"\r\n\r\nYou look over the supplies again. \"How much?\"\r\n\r\n\"At least four tons. Two Hundred shells.\"\r\n\r\nYou stare at him. \"Two Hundred shells?\"\r\n\r\nJarl nods enthusiastically. \"The fermentation went better than expected. Sheila's milk was exactly what the recipe required, and the lutefisk was prepared properly. With the mortar powder and the residue from the Smoker, we have everything necessary to produce a substantial supply of Smokey Lutefisk Ammo for the Lutefisk Launcher.\"\r\n\r\nYou glance toward the open cans of lutefisk. \"And you intend to fire all of that?\"\r\n\r\nJarl smiles. \"Eventually. The launcher has twenty-five tubes, Commander. It would be wasteful to build something like that and then run out of ammunition after a few volleys.\"\r\n\r\nYou take another breath and immediately regret it. \"Remind me why we are storing this in the Armory.\"\r\n\r\nJarl looks genuinely puzzled. \"Because it is ammunition?\"\r\n\r\nYou decide there are some questions that are better left unanswered.",
        "Icon": "uixTxrSpot_JarlAmmo.png"
    },
